# ── Never in a school image ─────────────────────────────────
# A school's database. `data` alone matches only the top level, so the
# glob is spelled out — a stray nested data/ directory would otherwise
# be copied into the image.
data
**/data

# The control plane. It is a SEPARATE deployment that merely shares this
# repository, and it has no business on a school's machine:
#
#   • sysadmin/data/registry.db holds the operator's password hash, TOTP
#     secret and recovery-code hashes — the credentials guarding EVERY
#     school. .gitignore keeps it out of git, but a Docker build context
#     ignores .gitignore entirely, so without this line it ships.
#   • serve.js already refuses to serve /sysadmin over HTTP (PRIVATE),
#     but code that is not in the image cannot be served, executed or
#     read at all.
#
# See sysadmin/README.md rule 1: the dependency arrow points one way.
sysadmin

# Documentation and artwork — no reason to be in a running container.
design
marketing
